    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0633" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6111/1141: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Second Secretary of Embassy in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thompson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Moscow</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-20T18:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>234. Reference Embassy’s 307, August 18, 11 a.m., from Moscow. The two Soviet
                    couriers are scheduled to depart August 21 by way of Brazil and Africa together
                    with Mrs. Oumansky<anchor n="32" xml:id="d525-f1"/> and daughter.</p>
                <p>The War Department has informally agreed to make available air accommodations for
                    two Soviet couriers every other month as desired by the Soviet Government, and
                    formal reply to the Department’s request in this regard is expected soon.<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d525-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d525-f1" n="32" xml:id="d525-f1-content">
                <p>Wife of Konstantin Alexandrovich Umansky, Soviet Ambassador in the United States,
                    1939–41.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d525-f2" n="33" xml:id="d525-f2-content">
                <p>This agreement for the travel of Soviet couriers between Washington and Tehran in
                    the airplanes of the Air Transport Command was received in a letter of September
                    8, 1942, from Henry L. Stimson, Secretary of War (701.6111/1145).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
